1
00:00:01,733 --> 00:00:04,245
In this video, we're going to talk about

2
00:00:04,245 --> 00:00:06,521
asthma, and what happens inside the

3
00:00:06,521 --> 00:00:10,929
airways. By the end of this video, you'll

4
00:00:10,929 --> 00:00:12,991
know exactly what asthma is.

5
00:00:14,193 --> 00:00:15,768
You'll know where in the airways it

6
00:00:15,768 --> 00:00:19,248
happens. You'll know what happens during

7
00:00:19,248 --> 00:00:22,780
an attack. And you'll know how reliever

8
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:24,705
and preventer inhalers help.

9
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:30,925
Here's someone out for a walk, breathing

10
00:00:30,925 --> 00:00:34,486
easily! Then something changes:

11
00:00:34,486 --> 00:00:36,749
the chest tightens, and breathing gets

12
00:00:36,749 --> 00:00:40,814
hard. Something has happened inside the

13
00:00:40,814 --> 00:00:44,635
airways. So what's going on in there?

14
00:00:48,400 --> 00:00:50,450
Asthma is a long-term condition of the

15
00:00:50,450 --> 00:00:53,263
airways: the tubes that carry air into and

16
00:00:53,263 --> 00:00:54,350
out of the lungs.

17
00:00:55,568 --> 00:00:58,080
It affects the bronchi, and the smaller

18
00:00:58,080 --> 00:01:00,780
airways beyond them, called bronchioles.

19
00:01:02,040 --> 00:01:04,028
Let's zoom into one of these small

20
00:01:04,028 --> 00:01:07,855
airways! This is where asthma lives:

21
00:01:07,893 --> 00:01:10,393
chronic inflammation of the airway wall.

22
00:01:14,167 --> 00:01:16,617
When the airway reacts to a trigger, three

23
00:01:16,617 --> 00:01:18,079
things happen together.

24
00:01:19,295 --> 00:01:21,858
The muscle ring around the wall tightens.

25
00:01:23,103 --> 00:01:25,578
The lining swells and becomes inflamed.

26
00:01:26,815 --> 00:01:29,227
And the airway produces extra, thick

27
00:01:29,227 --> 00:01:33,821
mucus. Watch how much less air can now get

28
00:01:33,821 --> 00:01:35,321
through this narrowed airway.

29
00:01:39,100 --> 00:01:41,375
This narrowing produces the symptoms of

30
00:01:41,375 --> 00:01:45,776
asthma. Wheezing, a whistling sound as air

31
00:01:45,776 --> 00:01:46,963
squeezes through.

32
00:01:48,204 --> 00:01:50,929
Breathlessness, a shortness of breath.

33
00:01:52,204 --> 00:01:54,004
A tight feeling in the chest.

34
00:01:55,220 --> 00:01:59,979
And a cough. Symptoms can vary over time,

35
00:01:59,992 --> 00:02:01,742
and are often worse at night.

36
00:02:05,567 --> 00:02:07,192
Different things can trigger these

37
00:02:07,192 --> 00:02:11,481
airways. Allergens, like pollen and dust

38
00:02:11,481 --> 00:02:14,710
mites. Tobacco smoke.

39
00:02:15,911 --> 00:02:17,736
Cold air can trigger them too.

40
00:02:18,927 --> 00:02:22,485
So can exercise. And respiratory

41
00:02:22,485 --> 00:02:26,755
infections. A trigger for one person may

42
00:02:26,755 --> 00:02:29,380
not affect another, but each one can set

43
00:02:29,380 --> 00:02:30,818
off the same narrowing.

44
00:02:34,567 --> 00:02:36,742
A reliever inhaler relieves symptoms

45
00:02:36,742 --> 00:02:40,601
quickly. A puff of mist is breathed in,

46
00:02:40,614 --> 00:02:42,689
and it acts fast on the airway:

47
00:02:42,689 --> 00:02:44,939
the tightened muscle relaxes, and the

48
00:02:44,939 --> 00:02:49,225
lumen reopens. But a reliever does not

49
00:02:49,225 --> 00:02:51,188
treat the underlying inflammation.

50
00:02:54,900 --> 00:02:57,550
A preventer inhaler works differently.

51
00:02:58,756 --> 00:03:01,768
It is taken daily, at home, not just when

52
00:03:01,768 --> 00:03:05,845
symptoms strike. Used every day, it

53
00:03:05,845 --> 00:03:08,308
reduces inflammation in the airway over

54
00:03:08,308 --> 00:03:12,878
time. With regular use, the swollen lining

55
00:03:12,878 --> 00:03:15,803
calms, day after day, even when feeling

56
00:03:15,803 --> 00:03:16,365
well.

57
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:22,150
A common mistake sounds like this:

58
00:03:22,163 --> 00:03:25,338
I feel fine, so I stopped my preventer,

59
00:03:25,400 --> 00:03:27,875
and just use the reliever when I need it.

60
00:03:29,092 --> 00:03:31,480
But overreliance on the reliever, with the

61
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,742
preventer skipped, is linked to poorer

62
00:03:33,742 --> 00:03:36,305
control and a higher risk of attacks.

63
00:03:38,032 --> 00:03:40,444
The preventer should be taken every day,

64
00:03:40,544 --> 00:03:42,732
even when feeling well, and inhaler

65
00:03:42,732 --> 00:03:44,757
technique should be checked regularly.

66
00:03:48,533 --> 00:03:49,933
Time for a quick check.

67
00:03:51,165 --> 00:03:53,828
During an asthma attack, three changes

68
00:03:53,828 --> 00:03:55,577
narrow this airway together.

69
00:03:56,821 --> 00:04:00,656
What are they? Pause the video, and think

70
00:04:00,656 --> 00:04:01,331
it through.

71
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:13,208
Together, three changes narrow the airway.

72
00:04:14,425 --> 00:04:16,637
The muscle tightens around the wall.

73
00:04:17,873 --> 00:04:20,186
The lining swells with inflammation.

74
00:04:21,345 --> 00:04:23,408
And thick mucus fills the lumen.

75
00:04:27,167 --> 00:04:30,721
Let's recap! Asthma is chronic

76
00:04:30,721 --> 00:04:32,484
inflammation of the airways.

77
00:04:33,679 --> 00:04:36,229
In an attack, the muscle tightens, the

78
00:04:36,229 --> 00:04:39,242
lining swells, and mucus fills the lumen,

79
00:04:39,292 --> 00:04:40,717
narrowing the airway.

80
00:04:41,927 --> 00:04:44,540
The reliever inhaler works fast, and the

81
00:04:44,540 --> 00:04:46,877
preventer inhaler works daily.

82
00:04:48,587 --> 00:04:51,237
Know your triggers, and use both inhalers

83
00:04:51,237 --> 00:04:52,299
as prescribed.

